        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c56ba80a-24b2-5911-9689-16742619a484",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gioachino Rossini, Andrea Leone Tottola, Francesco Ringhieri, Gaetano Donizetti, Sonia Ganassi\n- Works: Mosè in Egitto, Lucrezia Borgia, L'Osiride, Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra, La donna del lago, Ermione\n- Organizations/Events: ROF, Rossini in Wildbad\n\nFacts:\n- In 1760, Francesco Ringhieri wrote the play L'Osiride.\n- Mosè in Egitto is a three-act opera by Gioachino Rossini.\n- Mosè in Egitto has an Italian libretto by Andrea Leone Tottola.\n- Mosè in Egitto was based on Francesco Ringhieri's 1760 play L'Osiride.\n- Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\n- In 2004, Sonia Ganassi sang Elisabetta in Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra at ROF.\n- In 2006, Sonia Ganassi sang Elena in La donna del lago at Rossini in Wildbad.\n- In 2008, Sonia Ganassi performed in Ermione at ROF.\n- In 2011, Sonia Ganassi sang Elcia in Mosè in Egitto at ROF.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "06342852-1833-5564-9156-a991763a20a1",
        "text": "Page: Mosè in Egitto. Sentence: Mosè in Egitto (\"Moses in Egypt)\" (] ) is a three-act opera written by Gioachino Rossini to an Italian libretto by Andrea Leone Tottola, which was based on a 1760 play by Francesco Ringhieri, \"L'Osiride\".\nPage: Lucrezia Borgia (opera). Sentence: Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\nPage: Sonia Ganassi. Sentence: Her roles in Rossini operas include Elisabetta in \"Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra\" (ROF, 2004), Elena in \"La donna del lago (Lady of the Lake)\" (Rossini in Wildbad, 2006), \"Ermione\" (ROF, 2008), and Elcia in \"Mosè in Egitto\" (ROF, 2011).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
